-- ============================================================================
-- FC9 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Corrosion & Integrity, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: WHAT THE SCREEN ANSWERS AND WHAT IT WITHDREW. One
-- mechanism and one general uniform rate; the sour-service severity region
-- the engine no longer provides, and says so in two fields; the numbers with
-- no source; the units the engine speaks and the one studio factor that is
-- truncated; partial pressure against fugacity and which quantity drives
-- which answer; the two resistances in series; the protective film and an
-- onset that MOVES with fugacity; pH taken against a reference below which
-- the engine refuses; the wetting regime; and the studio's own default case
-- walked end to end.
--
-- THE HEADLINE OF THE WHOLE COURSE STARTS HERE. A curve carrying a standard's
-- name and telling an engineer what steel to buy was invented in an earlier
-- version of this engine, and the repair WITHDREW it rather than retuning it.
-- `regionProvided` and `materialGuidanceProvided` come back false on every
-- screening. That absence is current and permanent, and this tier teaches it
-- as the first thing to know about the app.
--
-- WHAT IS NEVER GRADED, IN ANY TIER: no corrosion rate the correlation
-- produced, no band label, no threshold verdict, no severity region, no
-- material choice. Eleven items are held for literature and the engine lists
-- them itself. The Associate capstone grades the stream bookkeeping, this
-- module's Reynolds number as a definition, and the corrosion inhibitor
-- arithmetic over two typed percentages, all in the engine's own units.
-- ============================================================================

